<resources>
    <string name="st_a11y_title">Accessibility service</string>
    <string name="st_a11y_on">Running. The capsule appears over other apps when something happens, such as a charger, a notification or music. To keep it always visible, turn on \"Always show pill\" in the Capsule tab.</string>
    <string name="st_a11y_off">Off. Turn on Capsool in Accessibility settings to show the capsule.</string>
    <string name="st_a11y_open">Open Accessibility settings</string>
    <string name="st_notif_title">Notification access</string>
    <string name="st_notif_on">On. The capsule can follow music and video players.</string>
    <string name="st_notif_off">Off. Needed to show what is playing and control it from the capsule. Capsool reads notifications on your phone only and never stores their text.</string>
    <string name="st_notif_allow">Allow notification access</string>
    <string name="st_restricted_title">Option greyed out?</string>
    <string name="st_restricted_body">On Android 13+ apps installed outside the Play Store are blocked from Accessibility and notification access. Open App info, tap ⋮ and choose \"Allow restricted settings\", then try again.</string>
    <string name="st_restricted_open">Open App info</string>
    <string name="st_ap_title">Advanced Protection is on</string>
    <string name="st_ap_body">Android Advanced Protection can switch off accessibility services that are not assistive tools, which stops the capsule. Capsool cannot work around this.</string>
    <string name="st_keepalive_title">Keep the capsule running</string>
    <string name="st_keepalive_body">Some phones stop background apps to save battery, which makes the capsule disappear. Follow these steps once.</string>
